WEBVTT

00:06.082 --> 00:09.024
I know it very well.

00:09.099 --> 00:14.037
You're the kindest
and bravest person I know.

00:21.013 --> 00:22.054
Well then.

00:23.007 --> 00:24.012
Goodbye.

00:36.003 --> 00:39.056
Elfie! I'll definitely climb the Tower!

00:39.056 --> 00:41.015
Even if I can't use magic!

00:41.052 --> 00:44.065
Even if many things are trying
to separate us together!

00:45.007 --> 00:47.009
I'll definitely come to you!

00:48.033 --> 00:50.066
This is my promise to you.

00:53.054 --> 00:55.007
Let's watch the sunset together!

01:00.048 --> 01:01.031
Yes.

01:02.033 --> 01:03.052
This is a promise.

01:04.084 --> 01:09.001
I'll always and always
be waiting for you.

01:17.047 --> 01:18.039
Will.

01:23.073 --> 01:26.001
Professor Workner...

01:29.044 --> 01:38.001
This is going to be the last time
I cry aloud in a miserable voice.

03:01.012 --> 03:04.037
EPISODE 3: ORDER & WATCHER

03:10.000 --> 03:13.097
URBUS RIGARDEN

03:14.088 --> 03:18.085
SLUMLAND STREET

03:18.085 --> 03:20.093
Will Serfort.

03:20.093 --> 03:25.094
A no-talent and an overachieving
book learner.

03:26.073 --> 03:28.019
FAMILIAR, KIKI

03:29.094 --> 03:31.057
Also a self-supported student.

03:31.098 --> 03:32.069
6TH-YEAR STUDENT OF THE RIGARDEN MAGICAL ACADEMY,
WILL SERFORT

03:32.069 --> 03:35.004
Hey, Will!
Early as ever, I see.

03:35.004 --> 03:36.095
Good morning, Donnan!

03:37.029 --> 03:37.095
Keep up the good work!

03:37.095 --> 03:39.002
DONNAN
Keep up the good work!

03:39.002 --> 03:41.033
DONNAN
I'll see you later at Gina's place.

03:41.074 --> 03:43.002
I'll be waiting!

03:57.034 --> 03:59.015
Oh, no...

04:04.068 --> 04:09.048
"Elfaria, the Albis Vina,
invented a new magic."

04:09.048 --> 04:13.044
"A record of twelve original spells
by a single mage."

04:13.099 --> 04:16.019
You're working hard, Elfie.

04:16.019 --> 04:17.092
I need to keep working hard too.

04:21.007 --> 04:25.054
"Along with this, the Upper Institute
has placed an order to the Academy."

04:25.054 --> 04:28.096
"The client is Elfaria herself."

04:28.096 --> 04:32.096
Wait, what?!

04:32.096 --> 04:34.096
OUTSKIRTS OF THE RIGARDEN DORMITORY

04:36.001 --> 04:38.000
6TH-YEAR STUDENT OF THE RIGARDEN MAGICAL ACADEMY
Rosty! Rosty!

04:38.000 --> 04:38.097
ROSTY NOWMAN
Rosty! Rosty!

04:39.039 --> 04:41.097
Rosty! Can you prepare
a magic item for me?

04:42.055 --> 04:45.085
What's up, Will?
Why the hurry?

04:46.005 --> 04:48.052
Elfie has placed an order.

04:48.052 --> 04:49.006
I have to go.

04:49.006 --> 04:52.004
And what about classes?

04:52.004 --> 04:54.061
I don't take any today.

04:54.061 --> 04:56.041
That's why I can prioritize this.

04:57.069 --> 04:58.086
Does it seem hard?

04:59.023 --> 05:02.028
The order is to gather ice cores
from the Frost Walkers.

05:02.028 --> 05:04.078
Apparently, she needs a lot of
magical catalysts.

05:04.078 --> 05:07.037
The students will get paid for
any amounts they can gather.

05:07.037 --> 05:12.096
I'm going to the fourth floor,
that's why I need your magic items!

05:15.025 --> 05:18.097
You're really an honest roommate.

05:19.029 --> 05:21.072
I've made some upgrades
since last time.

05:22.015 --> 05:23.072
Here you go.

05:23.072 --> 05:26.072
As expected of an artificer!
Thanks a lot!

05:30.001 --> 05:31.014
Will!

05:31.014 --> 05:34.083
Yeah?

05:34.083 --> 05:36.061
Take care.

05:38.065 --> 05:40.000
See you later!

05:42.045 --> 05:46.091
The great ancestor, the Mage Queen
Mercedes, once said this:

05:46.091 --> 05:49.049
"Everything comes from the dungeon."

05:51.008 --> 05:55.042
"O children of magic, venture forth
with knowledge and wisdom."

05:56.029 --> 05:59.021
"Conquer the unknown along your path."

05:59.021 --> 06:01.059
"Everything is connected."

06:03.088 --> 06:07.064
THE DUNGEON 4TH FLOOR

06:16.006 --> 06:18.065
This place is in total chaos.

06:18.065 --> 06:21.036
It's Elfie's order, after all.

06:21.036 --> 06:23.009
All right, Kiki, we go too—

06:27.078 --> 06:28.078
That's Sion for you!

06:28.078 --> 06:29.054
LYRIL MARS - SION ULSTER - GORDON VALLEY
That's Sion for you!

06:29.054 --> 06:32.071
LYRIL MARS - SION ULSTER - GORDON VALLEY
You blew those Frost Walkers to pieces!

06:34.025 --> 06:36.029
These small fries won't cut it.

06:36.083 --> 06:39.038
That time, he was more...

06:42.026 --> 06:44.043
Sion is amazing.

06:44.043 --> 06:46.068
But I somehow feel his bloodlust.

06:47.026 --> 06:49.097
If he's like that,
there won't be any monsters left here.

06:49.097 --> 06:52.022
I'll just have to go further down.

07:01.053 --> 07:02.009
Watch out!

07:19.084 --> 07:21.096
What just happened?

07:22.039 --> 07:26.047
Wait, that wasn't magic,
but a swordplay?

07:26.047 --> 07:28.047
Are you okay? Any injuries?

07:28.047 --> 07:30.055
No! I'm fine!

07:30.055 --> 07:33.031
Thank you for saving me.

07:34.027 --> 07:35.077
I'm glad.

07:35.077 --> 07:38.035
I'm Will, and you are?

07:39.083 --> 07:41.041
4TH-YEAR STUDENT OF THE RIGARDEN MAGICAL ACADEMY
My name is Iris.

07:41.041 --> 07:42.011
IRIS CHURCHILL

07:48.003 --> 07:49.085
PROFESSOR OF THE RIGARDEN MAGICAL ACADEMY
In this world,

07:49.085 --> 07:52.087
WORKNER NORGRAM
the creation of new magic is a great achievement.

07:53.033 --> 07:55.079
It's so great that it allows one

07:55.079 --> 07:59.038
ROSE PREHNITE - COLETTE LOIRE
to advance to the Tower unconditionally.

07:59.038 --> 08:06.051
New magic is often named after its creator
or a word associated with that person.

08:07.005 --> 08:10.039
For example, the dark magic,
Dax Darbicans.

08:10.039 --> 08:15.014
It's named after the ancient mage
Darbicans, the Keeper of Fire.

08:15.081 --> 08:22.052
If one of you could create new magic,
you would leave your mark on history.

08:22.052 --> 08:24.086
It sounds easy.

08:24.086 --> 08:28.078
But it's not a very realistic way
to advance.

08:29.019 --> 08:30.057
Professor Workner!

08:30.057 --> 08:35.041
Isn't the thing about Lady Elfaria from
this morning's newspaper amazing, then?

08:35.087 --> 08:38.037
If I put it into words...

08:38.037 --> 08:40.012
She's incredibly amazing.

08:40.012 --> 08:42.026
In fact, it's almost unbelievable.

08:44.009 --> 08:48.092
I've never even heard of an individual
creating twelve new magic.

08:49.034 --> 08:50.059
In that respect,

08:50.059 --> 08:55.025
she can be called the greatest mage
in the long history of the world.

08:56.002 --> 08:57.081
Lady Elfaria is really amazing.

08:57.081 --> 09:00.073
Does that mean ice magic
is the greatest now?

09:00.073 --> 09:03.044
I'm definitely going to the Ice Faction.

09:03.044 --> 09:08.036
The childhood friend that Will chases
is such an amazing person.

09:08.036 --> 09:11.095
Even now, the whole academy
is buzzing because of her order.

09:12.004 --> 09:15.002
Ah, you're looking like
a damsel in distress.

09:15.064 --> 09:18.058
A damsel?
What do you mean by that, Rose?

09:18.058 --> 09:21.058
You're jealous of Lady Elfaria,
aren't you?

09:21.058 --> 09:25.004
"His amazing childhood friend is going
to steal Will from me!" like that.

09:25.063 --> 09:27.003
Don't be silly!

09:27.003 --> 09:30.076
You two, don't be noisy!
We're in the middle of a lesson!

09:30.076 --> 09:33.009
I'm sorry, Professor Workner!

09:33.009 --> 09:34.061
I'm sorry!

09:35.076 --> 09:37.026
We got scolded.

09:37.026 --> 09:38.057
Good grief.

09:41.002 --> 09:45.082
Is he going to the dungeon today
for her sake?

09:45.082 --> 09:49.044
You must be that book learner.

09:49.044 --> 09:53.002
The senior who can't use magic,
the academy's first-ever no-talent.

09:53.002 --> 09:55.045
The first-ever, huh...

09:55.045 --> 09:57.058
Why did you call me senior?

09:57.058 --> 09:59.007
I'm fourteen.

10:00.016 --> 10:02.041
Two years younger than me.

10:02.041 --> 10:04.005
She's a fourth-year then.

10:04.005 --> 10:08.017
Doesn't it bother you?

10:08.017 --> 10:08.096
Huh?

10:08.096 --> 10:12.034
Like you said, I'm a no-talent.

10:12.034 --> 10:14.059
Aren't you uncomfortable?

10:16.047 --> 10:20.072
Why would I look down on my savior?

10:22.005 --> 10:26.023
You may not be able to use magic,
but you do have talent.

10:26.023 --> 10:29.000
And I respect that.

10:30.009 --> 10:33.007
Are you here for the order as well?

10:33.007 --> 10:37.007
Yes! I want to help Magia Vanders.

10:37.007 --> 10:40.062
I want to do my part to hold up the sky.

10:44.004 --> 10:47.008
What Iris said is not an exaggeration.

10:49.092 --> 10:52.092
We've never seen the real sky.

10:54.017 --> 11:00.019
The sky hanging over this world now
is a false sky, an enormous barrier,

11:00.081 --> 11:03.079
that Magia Vanders have put up
with their powerful magic.

11:06.048 --> 11:08.002
According to the Lore,

11:08.002 --> 11:12.044
when the barrier fails, the world will be
plunged into darkness once more.

11:12.044 --> 11:14.091
Then, the Calamity will begin.

11:15.065 --> 11:20.085
We students want to clear the orders not
just because we admire Magia Vanders.

11:20.085 --> 11:24.067
It's also because we believe
we're doing our part to hold up the sky.

11:26.071 --> 11:27.096
Senior Will!

11:28.058 --> 11:33.009
The truth is,
I have met Lady Elfaria.

11:33.009 --> 11:34.047
Huh? Really?

11:34.047 --> 11:36.063
Yes. I'll never forget it.

11:36.063 --> 11:41.001
That was when I was all alone
in the dungeon, and I was in danger.

11:41.001 --> 11:43.097
Iris, you get in danger a lot, huh?

11:44.041 --> 11:49.023
Surrounded by monsters. All alone.
It was a desperate situation.

11:49.067 --> 11:52.098
Just when I had death on my mind...

12:08.075 --> 12:10.029
Are you okay?

12:18.063 --> 12:21.014
Be careful next time.

12:23.006 --> 12:26.006
That's what happened to me!

12:26.006 --> 12:28.002
I see.

12:28.002 --> 12:31.043
Yes! And we talked about
a lot of things.

12:31.093 --> 12:34.027
Oh! Lady Elfaria!

12:34.027 --> 12:37.086
I will dedicate my life to you!

12:41.028 --> 12:45.045
And now, I was so excited about
the order and came down here,

12:45.045 --> 12:48.066
but I haven't found
a single Frost Walker.

12:48.066 --> 12:52.029
The others must have
taken them all out.

12:52.029 --> 12:55.008
My Search isn't picking up
anything either.

13:01.038 --> 13:04.001
Senior? What are you doing?

13:04.001 --> 13:08.031
Frost Walkers leave ice shards
in their tracks.

13:08.031 --> 13:10.087
Usually, the size is between
0.5 and 1 mille wide.

13:11.052 --> 13:15.009
But these are more than double that.

13:19.065 --> 13:22.026
There must be a colossal one up ahead.

13:22.078 --> 13:24.058
A colossal?

13:24.058 --> 13:25.049
Yeah.

13:25.049 --> 13:28.062
Probably somewhere your Search
can't reach.

13:28.062 --> 13:34.079
Wait! You can't use magic, right?
How can you know that?

13:35.046 --> 13:39.003
Magic is great, but it's not absolute.

13:39.008 --> 13:42.009
Especially not in the dungeon.

13:44.065 --> 13:50.093
Besides, even I can make up for it with
wisdom, knowledge, and experience.

13:51.006 --> 13:53.019
That's what I believe.

13:57.007 --> 13:59.003
Experience?

13:59.003 --> 14:00.019
Right.

14:03.078 --> 14:05.091
Knowing the unknown.

14:16.005 --> 14:17.071
That is...

14:24.018 --> 14:25.086
A Frost Rex!

14:27.001 --> 14:28.097
I knew it.

14:28.097 --> 14:30.043
It's a colossal.

14:48.049 --> 14:50.033
A Frost Rex.

14:50.033 --> 14:52.005
It's an advanced subspecies of
Frost Walker.

14:52.091 --> 14:56.000
An Over-Five Enemy is worth six credits.

14:56.036 --> 14:58.002
The fourth floor's Notorious Monster.

15:09.001 --> 15:10.072
You stay here, Iris.

15:11.035 --> 15:12.089
Don't!

15:12.089 --> 15:15.085
Physical attacks won't work
on Frost Rex.

15:15.085 --> 15:20.044
That's the dwarf killer.
It can freeze you if it touches you.

15:20.044 --> 15:23.086
The only measure is to use
ranged magic.

15:23.086 --> 15:25.086
It's too much for you!

15:26.057 --> 15:27.087
Don't worry.

15:32.062 --> 15:34.000
I've beaten that thing...

15:35.005 --> 15:37.005
...so many times already.

17:07.063 --> 17:11.026
Frost Rex is weak against fire.

17:17.045 --> 17:19.035
In other words, explosives.

17:55.085 --> 17:57.072
Torus Navalde!

18:35.068 --> 18:38.051
Rosty's magic items are incredible.

18:38.093 --> 18:40.077
I'll be sure to thank him later.

18:45.078 --> 18:48.004
I see. So this is the no-talent.

18:48.082 --> 18:52.094
There's a big difference
between rumors and reality.

18:53.007 --> 18:56.003
How should I report this?

18:56.065 --> 18:57.061
Iris!

18:58.041 --> 19:01.041
We got a lot of it.
Let's head back!

19:04.066 --> 19:05.096
Yes!

20:37.088 --> 20:41.051
MERCEDES CAULIS

20:45.039 --> 20:49.002
Since he can't use magic, he makes it up
with creativity and ingenuity.

20:49.044 --> 20:53.046
Not to mention, a battle sense
that can only come from experiences.

20:56.053 --> 21:01.082
Indeed, he's not a mage,
but a talented warrior.

21:07.002 --> 21:08.074
Excuse me.

21:17.092 --> 21:20.076
May I have a moment of your time?

21:20.076 --> 21:22.001
CARIOT INCINDIA WISEMAN
Magia Vanders.

21:22.001 --> 21:23.026
ELLENOR LJOS ALF

21:23.026 --> 21:24.051
ZEO THORZEUS REINBOLT

21:24.051 --> 21:26.001
ELFARIA ALBIS SERFORT

21:26.049 --> 21:28.052
Am I disturbing your time?

21:28.052 --> 21:33.025
Not at all, just the usual
insignificant meeting.

21:33.085 --> 21:37.028
Because if the barrier were breached,
the world would be destroyed by now.

21:37.065 --> 21:42.041
I'll bet those Celestial Hosts are just
over the other side watching us.

21:42.041 --> 21:45.077
We haven't got the numbers
or the strength to fight them.

21:46.065 --> 21:50.047
We need more elite mages
for the Fated Day.

21:50.047 --> 21:53.029
We won't allow the Lore
to become reality.

21:53.029 --> 21:57.021
How's everything on your side, Watcher?
You found anyone worth using?

21:57.021 --> 22:01.072
During my search at the Academy,
I found an interesting prospect.

22:01.072 --> 22:04.047
A no-talent who can't use magic.

22:05.003 --> 22:06.097
His name is Will Serfort.

22:07.045 --> 22:09.072
I recommend that he be brought
into the Tower.

22:09.072 --> 22:10.081
- Out of the question.
- Nope.

22:10.081 --> 22:11.098
That's interesting!

22:15.015 --> 22:18.086
I don't want more inferior goods
near me.

22:18.086 --> 22:20.074
I simply couldn't bear it.

22:20.074 --> 22:23.049
Both of you are so rigid.

22:23.049 --> 22:26.049
I'd even take a dwarf
if they were good.

22:26.049 --> 22:28.074
You'd take barbarians?

22:28.074 --> 22:33.005
I still can't see how a guy like you
can even be here in the first place.

22:34.037 --> 22:36.063
Enough, you two.

22:36.063 --> 22:39.063
In any case,
there's no need to be hasty.

22:40.026 --> 22:42.063
The Grand Magic Festival
is almost upon us.

22:43.005 --> 22:46.068
We can wait until then
to reach a decision.

22:46.068 --> 22:47.072
Sure.

22:47.072 --> 22:50.049
Talented people should find
their way to the top.

22:50.049 --> 22:53.081
And if they can't,
then that's it for them.

22:53.081 --> 22:56.065
The insignificant meeting is over, right?

22:56.065 --> 22:58.001
I'm going first.

23:09.058 --> 23:13.091
The boy you told me about,
he's really fascinating.

23:14.041 --> 23:16.017
Lady Elfaria.

23:25.038 --> 23:29.001
Will, I'll always be waiting for you.

23:38.002 --> 23:41.052
Next up, Episode 4 of
Wistoria: Wand and Sword,

23:41.094 --> 23:43.049
"Festival Eve."
